WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Every last inch of me's covered with hair!

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.940
Ohhhh Really?

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.100
Hello, Internet!

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.980
Welcome to film theory.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.900
Where today's little episode will teach you that

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.380
Not everything is ay-okay in Disney's fairy-tale universe.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.280
Case in point,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.160
One of my personal favorites:

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.380
Beauty and the beast.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.060
Similar to a lot of the classic movies like Snow White and Sleeping beauty,

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.900
"B and the B" Opens with a storybook-style preface

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.580
That dumps a whole bunch of exposition on the audience.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.300
Meaning the kiddies don't have to shlep through a bunch of backstory

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.940
before they get to the singing tea cups and promiscuous feather-duster.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.260
In it, we're treated to a story bout an arrogant, shallow prince

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.660
living in a castle that's visited by an old beggar woman on a cold winter's night.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.300
She's looking for a place to stay,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.840
and then tries to trade him a rose in exchange for a night out of the weather.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.980
According to the story, he turns up his nose at her rose,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.820
and is so put off by how old and ugly she is,

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.580
that he refuses to let her in.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.820
She warns him that real beauty comes from the inside,

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.060
And that he shouldn't be swayed by appearances

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.320
But he's having none of it and tells her to get lost.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.560
At that point, she changes into a beautiful sorceress and the prince sees that he's made a huge mistake.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.220
"You've made a huge mistake."

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.000
But, his apologies come too late.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.700
In punishment for his arrogance,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.700
she turns him into the beast.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.240
So, what's the theory here?

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.260
Well, along with transforming him into a monster,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.220
the sorceress also gives him the rose he rejected.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.740
Which, surprise surprise, happens to be a magical rose.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.120
It comes with a catch that it'll bloom until he turns 21,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.820
at which point he's either had to have found someone who loves him,

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:31.320
OR

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.020
He'll stay a beast forever once that last pedal falls.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.880
Basically the most elaborate hourglass ever.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.200
Oh and, before she goes,

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.560
all the princes employees are turned into cutlery.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.080
Because of… reasons.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.880
So, ashamed of his looks and with 21 as the magic number,

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.860
the beast stays locked in his castle

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.500
with all his anthropomorphic household utensils.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.720
Which takes us to the point where the movie starts

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.760
and Belle stumbles in ready for some good-old fashioned Stockholm Syndrome.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.460
It's unclear how much time it's taken her to get there,

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:03.580
until Lumière gives it away in the song that'll be played in dinner theaters from now until eternity:

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:04.840
Be our guest.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.460
"Ohhh…"

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.640
"Ten years we've been rusting,"

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.120
"Needing so much more than dusting."

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.760
So, according to the lyrics of the song,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.600
we know that they've been rusting as household appliances for ten years.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.740
But-Wait a minute, how does that make any sense?

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:22.120
We know that when Belle shows up, the rose has "Already begun to wilt".

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.480
So we're in the home stretch towards the beast's twenty-first birthday.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.260
If they've been waiting for Belle for ten years,

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.300
that means that when the old woman shows up at his doorstep,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.360
the prince was…

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:32.980
AT

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:33.740
AT MOST:

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:34.640
ELEVEN

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.540
ELEVEN YEARS

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.180
ELEVEN YEARS OLD.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.900
And I know what you're going to say in the comments:

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:43.520
"But Matpat, those are song lyrics. They might just be hyperbolic representations of real story elements."

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.780
To which I would say:

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:45.460
"Wow,"

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:49.460
"What an incredibly well articulated response for the Youtube comments section."

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.600
But, here's my rebuttal:

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.180
Beauty and the beast is one of the best examples of a Disney movie leaning heavily on song lyrics

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.340
to forward major plot elements.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.100
It's only through the songs in the movie

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.900
that we learn how Belle dreams of finding more in her life,

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.840
How we learn that Gaston plans to hold Belle's father hostage,

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.620
AND how Belle and the beast are developing feelings for each other.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.640
Belle sings about her book reading habits,

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.760
Gaston sings about his tromping in boots and home decorating abilities,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.220
"I use antlers in all of my"

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.740
"DECORATING"

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:18.260
I mean,

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:18.840
Yes,

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.100
This COULD be a metaphor,

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:20.920
but Siriusly,

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.740
look at the antlers he's using in his home decor!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.120
Queer eye for the straight guy, this is not.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.860
These songs aren't about metaphor,

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:30.380
their lyrics are meant to be taken literally.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.740
They're about providing critical information about the characters AND their story.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.940
Which means Beauty and the beast's prologue isn't talking about just a young prince,

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.920
it's talking about a REALLY young prince.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.940
So, taking a look back at the movie opening again,

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.240
with the prince and the old woman,

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.720
we realize that the story we're being told is

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:48.320
FAAAAAAAAAAAAAR

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.360
Different from what actually happened.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.540
The beast didn't start as some Jerky, Arrogant member of a royal family,

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.960
In reality, the prince,

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.100
Who's young enough to still be watching power rangers, un-ironically mind you,

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.500
answers the door in the middle of the night

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:07.280
Which, as an aside, should actually fall on Cogsworth as the butler.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.060
#ButtleFail

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.280
Once there, this eleven-year-old boy finds a dirty old woman at the front door.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.620
She wants to come in, but he says no, because,

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:16.540
well, you know…

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.880
He's a little kid who's alone in the middle of the night!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.200
And she probably stinks of urine, and…

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.360
Forest wolf…

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.280
or something…

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.780
Those things were SO scary…

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.360
She offers him a rose, but he's not interested because,

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.900
well, can someone say "stranger danger"?

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:30.960
Don't accept candy

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.960
(Or creepy glowing floral arrangements)

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.480
from strangers, kiddos.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.080
"And knowing is half the battle."

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.240
And, when she turns into a beautiful sorceress,

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.400
He apologizes because he's a nice kid who didn't mean to offend her.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.760
But the sorceress apparently has a vendetta,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.480
showing no leniency to a kid who was doing what

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.300
ALL RESPONISBLE YOUNG KIDS

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.340
Should have done in that situation.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.200
She curses him by making him grow up as a monster.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.240
As if puberty didn't suck enough.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:01.420
Oh, and because she's really a lot more evil than Disney's storybook opening would have us believe,

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.520
she also happens to curse everyone else in the house…

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.400
because

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.400
why not?

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.540
Which probably be hatin' on some rich folks up in this hazzause.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.860
Then, over the next ten years,

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:11.640
he hides.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.120
even more than he would as a regular teenager.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.360
during that time, he develops a grand total of zero social skills,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.740
and doesn't even know how to begin when approaching a girl,

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.200
Much less getting one to fall in love with him.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.060
In his state of arrested development,

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.620
"I've made a huge mistake."

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:29.160
He doesn't know how to react when Belle's father shows up at the castle.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.500
And he behaves NOT like a rational adult,

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.360
but like a petulant child.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.100
Which is,

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:34.740
Which is, Surprise

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:35.860
Which is, Surprise (x2),

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.260
EXACTLY what he is.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.480
The beast isn't a monster!

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.160
He's not even a bad guy.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.040
He's just a little kid

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.520
who never had the chance to grow up.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.700
But hey,

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.000
that's just a theory!

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:50.500
a         theory!

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.220
a film theory!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.060
a film theory!

